<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John II of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1398–1479</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> by marriage from 1425 and King of Aragon from 1458 until his death. His conflict with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-prince-of-viana">Charles of Viana</a> and with the Catalan institutions led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-civil-war">Catalan Civil War</a> of 1462 to 1472, which he eventually won. He arranged the marriage of his son Ferdinand to Isabella of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, preparing the union of the Spanish crowns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="John II of Aragon" width="220" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SOAOTO_-_Folio_067R_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
